<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laus was an ancient Greek city on the Tyrrhenian coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, near the mouth of the Lao river in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, founded as a colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sybaris">Sybaris</a>. Near it, in 389 BCE, the Lucanians crushed an army of Thurii and its Italiote allies. The town later came under Lucanian control, and its remains have been excavated near Santa Maria del Cedro.</p></div>
